{"name":"Turkish Bath","hex":"#bb937b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bath","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tub or pool which is used for bathing: bathtub.","A building or area where bathing occurs."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wash a person or animal in a bath.","To bathe (oneself); to have a bath."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hammam","blocks":[{"text":"A hammam, also often called a Turkish bath by Westerners, is a type of steam bath or a place of public bathing associated with the Islamic world. It is a prominent feature in the culture of the Muslim world and was inherited from the model of the Roman thermae. Muslim bathhouses or hammams were historically found across the Middle East, North Africa, al-Andalus, Central Asia, the Indian subcontinent, and in Southeastern Europe under Ottoman rule."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Ali_Gholi_Agha_hammam%2C_Isfahan%2C_Iran.jpg/330px-Ali_Gholi_Agha_hammam%2C_Isfahan%2C_Iran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammam","wikidata":"Q28077"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG/500px-THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG/1280px-THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG/500px-THERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Remains of the Antonine Baths in ancient Carthage, from the Roman period, in present-day Tunisia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATHERMES_D_ANTONIN_7.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedi